  "id": "DrugBank_DB01367 - MONDO_10482",
  "verbalization": "Rasagiline is implicated in the pathogenesis of X-linked Parkinsonism-spasticity Syndrome through its role in the treatment of Atypical Juvenile Parkinsonism, a condition that is itself linked to the syndrome. The evidence suggests that Rasagiline acts as a therapeutic agent for Atypical Juvenile Parkinsonism, which in turn is associated with X-linked Parkinsonism-spasticity Syndrome. This relationship is supported by the shared indication of Rasagiline with multiple drugs that target similar pathophysiological mechanisms, such as Tolcapone, Pimavanserin, and Apomorphine. These drugs are all indicated for Atypical Juvenile Parkinsonism, and their association with X-linked Parkinsonism-spasticity Syndrome implies a potential mechanistic overlap, possibly involving neurodegenerative processes or neurotransmitter dysregulation. The integrated evidence highlights a possible pathway where Rasagiline, through its therapeutic effects on Atypical Juvenile Parkinsonism, contributes to the management of X-linked Parkinsonism-spasticity Syndrome, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
